==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Catclaw Castle (Enemy Base)|Catclaw Castle]].
*1 [[Metal Hippoe]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*5 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*3 [[Hippoe]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*3 [[Teacher Bear]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 66.67~70 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is noticeably more difficult than the previous stages, with buffed enemies supported by a Metal Hippoe. This stage emphasizes the importance of [[Treasure]]s, collecting drops from [[Empire of Cats]] stages that, when certain ones are collected, give you different boosts, whether that be worker cat rate, wallet, or your cat's stats.

You'll want to have several long-ranged attackers in your lineup, such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], as well as some critical hitters to deal with the Metal Hippoe, like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat]]. Despite being an easily accessible critical hitter, [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]] is not ideal for this stage due to her low range and critical hit chance. The Sir Seals in this stage act as supporting pushers, making it harder to take down the Metal Hippoe. They can be dealt with quickly by using anti-Red units such as [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cat]] or [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]]. Meatshield to protect your attackers, and winning would only be a matter of time.

==Hints==
These hints only appear as defeat messages upon losing the stage.
*Critical effects only activate occasionally.<br>Deploy multiple units with a Critical effect<br>to increase the chance of it activating.<br>Use your army to the fullest to finish the fight!
*Effects of Treasures collected from Empire<br>of Cats Ch. 1 carry over into Ch. 2. Slowly<br>but surely, you can build your humble army<br>into an unstoppable powerhouse!

